# TP.10: the edge tmux 3.7b draws round a window smaller than its client
# (what the outer client shows while a popup attaches to its own session):
# `│` down the right, `─` along the foot, `┘` at the corner and `┴` where
# a pane border meets it, the letterbox beyond. The status line is off.
$ new-session -d -s main -n first -x 40 -y 12 cat
$ set -g status off
client 40x12 attach -t main
$ resize-window -t main -x 30 -y 8
screen ┘
$ split-window -h -t main cat
screen ┴
$ split-window -v -t main cat
screen ┤
